 * Google v. Oracle directly affects SquirrelJME as it is a Java ME 8
   Virtual Machine and Runtime Library which is a clean-room reverse
   engineered project solely based on documentation and observed behaviors of
   existing software.
 * Considering that PhoneME, KVM, OpenJDK, and Android exist it would be
   impossible to determine if an AI has been trained on these projects or not.
 * SquirrelJME is not a non-profit and has a _Patreon_ along with sponsorships,
   although I am not doing this with the intention of making money there is
   always the possibility of a non-MPL licensed SquirrelJME being purchased
   by an enterprise corporation.

Therefor because of this, any use of AI is an existential threat to SquirrelJME
and the project as a whole, thusly any and all usage is permanently banned
until the appropriate time when this may be re-evaluated.

## Future Policy Reservation

Due to court rulings and/or opinions, considering the time, cost, and lack
of any existence of such AI technologies, this reservation is not being
considered at this time.

Permitted use of GenAI with SquirrelJME with only authorized tools may be 
accepted in the future, if all the following conditions are met along with
the main points of the [contributing.mkd](contributing.mkd) agreement:

 * The GenAI models are solely trained on SquirrelJME's source code, notes,
   history, and documentation. They must not be trained on any other data
   which is not in the public domain.
 * No generic models or additional models are applied, this includes additional
   models which provide support for human languages.
 * It must not train from any other source that is not SquirrelJME.
 * The use of the GenAI is run on the local device whether that be a CPU,
   GPU, or NPU without the use of an internet and network connection, it
   must be fully usable offline.
 * The models must be fully reproducible and deterministic, the same input
   must result in the same output.
 * The models must be able to be trained fully offline on the local device.
 * The model training, prompt, and all other related software must be under an
   Open Source Initiative (OSI) license.
 * All related software is able to be copyright, license, and trademark
   assigned to SquirrelJME in terms of full ownership with no restrictions.
   That is, it is donated to the project with no restrictions placed.
 * The tool has been vetted and approved by the administrators of SquirrelJME.

